    "voiceover_text": "Most people using AI... are making themselves slower. They type a vague prompt. Get a mediocre answer. Edit it for twenty minutes. And call that productivity. Here is the actual problem. ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini — none of them know anything about you. Your job. Your writing style. What you actually need. So every single conversation starts from zero. The people getting real output from AI? They have built what is called a system prompt. A permanent set of instructions the AI reads before you type anything. Your role. Your tone. What to avoid. What format you want answers in. Your writing style. All of it. Written once. I built mine six months ago. I have not edited a single AI output since. Most people never build one. Which means they do the same setup work. Every. Single. Session. That is not AI saving you time. That is AI costing you time. Build the prompt once.",
